{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/results.json | sed -n '44592,44646p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75f.md | tail -8; nl -ba poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-3/package.report.json; rg -n 'export_seconds|check_seconds' poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/*/package.report.json; rg -n 'def test.*occupied|FileExistsError' tests/test_release.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/results.json | sed -n '44592,44646p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75f.md | tail -8; nl -ba poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-3/package.report.json; rg -n 'export_seconds|check_seconds' poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/*/package.report.json; rg -n 'def test.*occupied|FileExistsError' tests/test_release.py\"","aggregated_output":" 44592\t    \"equal_to_store\": true,\n 44593\t    \"present\": true,\n 44594\t    \"holds_its_wording\": true\n 44595\t   }\n 44596\t  },\n 44597\t  \"implied_outcome_j1580\": \"About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-reven\",\n 44598\t  \"substituted_into_e2295_refused\": \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\",\n 44599\t  \"added_to_manifest_refused\": \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\",\n 44600\t  \"unchanged_package_passes\": 91055,\n 44601\t  \"forged_value_is_j1580\": true\n 44602\t },\n 44603\t \"old-1/v8\": {\n 44604\t  \"class\": \"number\",\n 44605\t  \"forecast\": \"Forecast unavailable\",\n 44606\t  \"evidence\": 1284,\n 44607\t  \"same_ids_as_service_evidence\": true\n 44608\t },\n 44609\t \"leaks\": {\n 44610\t  \"old-3/v36@2026-08-25\": {\n 44611\t   \"package_as_of\": \"2026-08-25\",\n 44612\t   \"manifest_as_of\": \"2026-08-25\",\n 44613\t   \"evidence\": 3239,\n 44614\t   \"latest_judgement\": 799,\n 44615\t   \"expected_judgement\": 799,\n 44616\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 44617\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 44618\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 44619\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 44620\t   \"phrase_fields\": {\n 44621\t    \"around $1 trillion\": [],\n 44622\t    \"rung 4\": [],\n 44623\t    \"at rung\": [],\n 44624\t    \"capex at rung\": []\n 44625\t   }\n 44626\t  },\n 44627\t  \"old-1/v10@2026-08-28\": {\n 44628\t   \"package_as_of\": \"2026-08-28\",\n 44629\t   \"manifest_as_of\": \"2026-08-28\",\n 44630\t   \"evidence\": 5673,\n 44631\t   \"latest_judgement\": 865,\n 44632\t   \"expected_judgement\": 865,\n 44633\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 44634\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 44635\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 44636\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 44637\t   \"phrase_fields\": {\n 44638\t    \"around $1 trillion\": [],\n 44639\t    \"rung 4\": [],\n 44640\t    \"at rung\": [],\n 44641\t    \"capex at rung\": []\n 44642\t   }\n 44643\t  }\n 44644\t },\n 44645\t \"control\": {\n 44646\t  \"id\": \"v3\",\n    10\t| A placeholder could stand in for the forecast, and Tests 8 and 10 accepted loose reasons | **The placeholder and both named refusal cases are closed.** I checked that both saved forgeries contain the full 315-character forecast from judgement 1580. The script itself verifies only a prefix. Tests 8 and 10 now require their exact messages. [release_check.py:191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:191) · [release_check.py:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:201) · [test_release.py:294](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:294) · [test_release.py:343](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:343) · [test_release.py:364](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:364) |\n    11\t\n    12\t### Two certification gaps\n    13\t\n    14\t1. **A September package can pass as an August release.** For `old-3`, the substitution increased the evidence count from 3,239 to 6,659. For `old-1`, it increased from 5,673 to 8,251. The script looks up the judgement on the requested August day, but never compares that day with the returned package’s `as_of`. Both September answers were still “Yes,” so every historical assertion passed. The saved August packages are correctly dated. The decisive check is to compare the returned package date with the requested day. [release_check.py:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:206) · [release_check.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:266) · [August 25 report:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23f/old-3/package-2026-08-25.report.json:11) · [August 28 report:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23f/old-1/package-2026-08-28.report.json:11)\n    15\t2. **The package can declare the wrong format or allow-list version and still be certified if a production constant drifts.** Revision 11 fixes both identifiers at `/1`. In two separate in-memory checks, I changed one constant and its corresponding package identifier to `/2`. Each passed all 91,055 `old-1` comparisons at the original byte size. The writer and checker share those constants, and the acceptance script checks neither identifier independently. A literal comparison of both identifiers on the delivered package closes this gap. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [release.py:157](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:157) · [release.py:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:296) · [release_check.py:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:254)\n    16\t\n    17\t**Optional under §5.** The blanket claim about *every* assertion is still too broad. The test helper takes its expected day from the export. Some occupied-path tests check only `FileExistsError` or exit status. These and the narrower quote scan do not independently let a wrong package through. The production builder already passes its separately resolved day into the staged check. I would stop after the two demonstrated certification gaps and verify them against the saved packages. All review work was read-only. [test_release.py:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:172) · [test_release.py:321](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:321) · [test_release.py:486](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:486) · [test_release.py:579](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:579) · [release_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:61)     1\t{\n     2\t \"ledger\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\",\n     3\t \"items\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\",\n     4\t \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\",\n     5\t \"counts\": {\n     6\t  \"questions\": {\n     7\t   \"number\": 18,\n     8\t   \"event\": 31,\n     9\t   \"yes_no\": 0\n    10\t  },\n    11\t  \"evidence\": 6659,\n    12\t  \"sources\": 6659,\n    13\t  \"fields_compared\": 73559\n    14\t },\n    15\t \"withheld_unresolved\": [],\n    16\t \"data_bytes\": 4685247,\n    17\t \"export_seconds\": 3.84,\n    18\t \"check_seconds\": 2.7\n    19\t}poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-3/package.report.json:17: \"export_seconds\": 3.84,\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-3/package.report.json:18: \"check_seconds\": 2.7\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-2/package.report.json:17: \"export_seconds\": 3.64,\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-2/package.report.json:18: \"check_seconds\": 2.55\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/served/package.report.json:17: \"export_seconds\": 2.5,\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/served/package.report.json:18: \"check_seconds\": 1.79\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1/package.report.json:17: \"export_seconds\": 4.73,\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1/package.report.json:18: \"check_seconds\": 3.32\n322:    with pytest.raises(FileExistsError):\n568:    with pytest.raises(FileExistsError):\n575:    with pytest.raises(FileExistsError):\n592:    assert code == 1 and f\"refused: FileExistsError: [Errno 17] File exists: '{late}'\" in err.splitlines()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"comple