{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**Slice 1 accepted.** Both round 75f gaps are closed. The saved packages passed the script’s final decision. Replaying the two previously accepted errors in memory now produces a failure in each case. No files were changed.\n\n1. **A September package fails an August check.** The August 25 package and its manifest both say August 25, and I counted 3,239 evidence entries. The August 28 package and its manifest both say August 28, with 5,673 entries. For each case, substituting the corresponding September 20 values failed. Changing only the package date or only the manifest date also failed, even with the correct August count and the answer still “Yes.” [release_check.py:219](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:219) · [release_check.py:276](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:276) · [results.json:44610](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/results.json:44610) · [results.json:44627](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/results.json:44627)\n\n2. **A `/2` identifier fails even when the production constant agrees.** All four default packages carry `hivemind-release/1` and `release-allow-list/1` in both data and manifest. On saved `old-1`, I changed the format to `/2` in the data, manifest and production constant together, then repeated the experiment for the allow-list. Both failed with `old-1: format or allow-list`. The final decision uses its own literals. Test 1 independently checks both literals on the export. [release_check.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:24) · [release_check.py:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:261) · [test_release.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:208)\n\n3. **The run supports the result page’s claims about both fixes and all four stores’ counts, sizes and timings.** One wording issue remains optional under §5. The page says *every* refusal is matched by its exact message, then correctly identifies tests that check only the error type or exit status. The unit-test and mutant totals are separate from this four-store run. [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:74](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:74) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:86) · [test_release.py:322](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:322) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:103](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:103)"}}
